A new difluorodiphenyl sulfone monomer containing pendent 3,5-dimethylphenyl groups was synthesized by a two-step reaction according to the similar method reported in our preceding studies (Scheme 1
                        ) [44]. Four pendant benzylmethyl groups in this monomer were designed as side chain sites for imidazolium-functionalization. The structure of Me-DFDPS was confirmed by NMR spectroscopy. Fig. 1
                         was the 1H NMR spectrum of Me-DFDPS. As shown in Fig. 1, the protons of methyl groups appeared at 2.38ppm and the aromatic protons appeared at 7.0–8.1ppm, respectively. The assignments of each proton agreed well with the proposed molecular structure, which indicated the successful preparation of the target monomer.

Long-term alkaline stability of AEMs is regarded as a crucial property for the application of AEMs in fuel cells, especially in strong basic and elevated temperature conditions. To investigate the chemical stability of PAES-Im-xx membranes in strong basic and elevated temperature conditions, they were immersed in a 4M NaOH solution at 80°C for two weeks (336h). During the testing period, PAES-Im-xx membranes could remain their original shape and flexibility (Fig. 7
                        ), but the control sample PAES-QA was brittle and unstable due to the degradation of QA groups. The alkaline stability of PAES-Im-xx membranes was further evaluated by measuring the changes of IEC and conductivity after treating (Table 3
                        ). As shown in Table 3, there is no obvious decreasing for their IEC values and conductivities after treating for 336h. The loss of IEC values was less than 5%. It should also be noted that no new chemical shifts of the tested membrane were observed in 1H NMR (Fig. 8
                        ). All results illustrate that these AEMs have excellent alkaline stability and could withstand corrosion in concentrated basic solutions at increased temperature.
